1
00:00:05,961 --> 00:00:08,442
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you ever run through a stop signal at second?

2
00:00:08,682 --> 00:00:10,343
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, yeah.

3
00:00:10,883 --> 00:00:12,984
[SPEAKER_02]: Not seeing it or just thinking you could get it?

4
00:00:13,425 --> 00:00:14,705
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't run with your head down.

5
00:00:15,786 --> 00:00:16,346
[SPEAKER_01]: You didn't see it?

6
00:00:16,706 --> 00:00:18,887
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't see the coach give me a stop sign the whole way.

7
00:00:20,692 --> 00:00:28,102
[SPEAKER_02]: When you run with your head down you can't see.

8
00:00:29,023 --> 00:00:31,266
[SPEAKER_01]: I had a pretty good question for him.

9
00:00:31,306 --> 00:00:33,109
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, well I thought I could make that for him.

10
00:00:33,189 --> 00:00:36,773
[SPEAKER_01]: I got a better chance on third base and I had one second to score.

11
00:00:38,462 --> 00:00:39,642
[SPEAKER_01]: Where you gonna score from now?

12
00:00:39,702 --> 00:00:40,902
[SPEAKER_01]: I said going back to Vince.

13
00:00:42,783 --> 00:00:45,163
[SPEAKER_02]: Were you out at any times you ran through the stop sign?

14
00:00:45,563 --> 00:00:45,803
[SPEAKER_02]: Huh?

15
00:00:45,823 --> 00:00:48,604
[SPEAKER_02]: Does it ever get you out at third when he's tripled?

16
00:00:48,684 --> 00:00:51,204
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, he got me out then when I ran through the stop line.

17
00:00:51,224 --> 00:00:52,004
[SPEAKER_01]: Going home, you mean?

18
00:00:52,444 --> 00:00:56,985
[SPEAKER_02]: No, I mean on plays where you didn't make a triple but you tried to and were thrown out at third.

19
00:00:57,465 --> 00:01:03,386
[SPEAKER_02]: Happened a few times, huh?

20
00:01:04,386 --> 00:01:06,467
[SPEAKER_01]: I'd like to talk about this 33 ball club.

21
00:01:06,487 --> 00:01:07,087
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, go ahead.

22
00:01:08,714 --> 00:01:13,802
[SPEAKER_01]: We started out the spring training with a Mohawk club, looked like a major league Mohawk club on paper.

23
00:01:14,864 --> 00:01:18,429
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I played right field and they had Terry Moore in center.

24
00:01:19,865 --> 00:01:21,566
[SPEAKER_01]: And Jack Rothrock played left field.

25
00:01:21,786 --> 00:01:22,126
[SPEAKER_01]: Jack?

26
00:01:22,446 --> 00:01:23,287
[SPEAKER_01]: Jack Rothrock.

27
00:01:23,347 --> 00:01:24,067
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, yeah.

28
00:01:24,127 --> 00:01:24,387
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

29
00:01:24,767 --> 00:01:28,189
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, first base he had Mickey Heath, second base was Burgess Friday.

30
00:01:28,669 --> 00:01:29,909
[SPEAKER_01]: Bill and Myers played short.

31
00:01:30,510 --> 00:01:31,810
[SPEAKER_01]: Lou Riggs played third base.

32
00:01:31,830 --> 00:01:33,011
[SPEAKER_02]: It was a big, big team, wasn't it?

33
00:01:33,071 --> 00:01:33,411
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

34
00:01:33,431 --> 00:01:35,932
[SPEAKER_01]: New Lansky and O'Day were the kickers.

35
00:01:36,232 --> 00:01:41,815
[SPEAKER_01]: And Paul Lee, Bill Lee, Jim Winford, Lefty Heisey.

36
00:01:42,175 --> 00:01:42,795
[SPEAKER_01]: Jim who?

37
00:01:43,155 --> 00:01:43,896
[SPEAKER_01]: Jim Winford.

38
00:01:45,936 --> 00:01:46,917
[SPEAKER_01]: Good kickers, yeah.

39
00:01:47,904 --> 00:01:56,047
[SPEAKER_01]: So we went on, we won the Pennant by 12 or 15 ballgames.

40
00:01:56,067 --> 00:02:06,310
[SPEAKER_01]: So eight boys off of the 33 ballclub were playing on a 34 ballclub with the Cardinals in the World Series.

41
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:08,950
[SPEAKER_01]: And they beat Detroit in the World Series.

42
00:02:08,990 --> 00:02:11,891
[SPEAKER_01]: Dizzy won two games and Paul won the other two and lost one.

43
00:02:12,532 --> 00:02:14,192
[SPEAKER_01]: But that was the ballclub we were in.

44
00:02:14,612 --> 00:02:15,372
[SPEAKER_02]: Who were the eight?

45
00:02:16,073 --> 00:02:16,333
[SPEAKER_01]: Huh?

46
00:02:16,413 --> 00:02:17,213
[SPEAKER_02]: Who were the eight?

47
00:02:18,652 --> 00:02:19,392
[SPEAKER_02]: Who were the what?

48
00:02:19,412 --> 00:02:20,193
[SPEAKER_02]: The eight players.

49
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:31,499
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, Galancy was one, Whitehead, Riggs, Rothrock, Terry Moore, Paul Dean, and Bill Weed.

50
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:33,440
[SPEAKER_02]: And O'Day maybe too?

51
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:35,101
[SPEAKER_01]: O'Day, yeah.

52
00:02:35,121 --> 00:02:35,942
[SPEAKER_01]: That's remarkable.

53
00:02:36,362 --> 00:02:37,342
[SPEAKER_01]: That's a good book, that.

54
00:02:37,382 --> 00:02:39,163
[SPEAKER_02]: How'd you do in the Junior World Series?

55
00:02:39,423 --> 00:02:40,704
[SPEAKER_02]: We won one of the World Series.

56
00:02:40,724 --> 00:02:41,364
[SPEAKER_02]: What'd you play?

57
00:02:41,825 --> 00:02:43,586
[SPEAKER_02]: Played Syracuse.

58
00:02:46,988 --> 00:02:47,628
[SPEAKER_02]: Four straight?

59
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:56,602
[SPEAKER_02]: Where did you live in Columbus at that time?

60
00:02:57,183 --> 00:03:00,644
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you move here permanently then?

61
00:03:00,664 --> 00:03:04,026
[SPEAKER_02]: Where did you spend the winter months in these years?

62
00:03:04,046 --> 00:03:05,567
[SPEAKER_02]: Right here in Columbus.

63
00:03:05,787 --> 00:03:07,288
[SPEAKER_02]: Say back in the 1920s.

64
00:03:07,988 --> 00:03:09,969
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, 1920s in South Dakota.

65
00:03:09,989 --> 00:03:11,630
[SPEAKER_01]: I lived in Madison, South Dakota.

66
00:03:11,650 --> 00:03:12,631
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, you made that your home?

67
00:03:12,771 --> 00:03:13,111
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

68
00:03:13,491 --> 00:03:14,472
[SPEAKER_01]: I lived there ten years.

69
00:03:15,492 --> 00:03:16,493
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you get married then?

70
00:03:16,653 --> 00:03:17,213
[SPEAKER_02]: Yes, I did.

71
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,441
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you marry a gal from up there?

72
00:03:19,501 --> 00:03:20,401
[SPEAKER_02]: I did, yeah.

73
00:03:21,782 --> 00:03:23,403
[SPEAKER_02]: Your family started up there?

74
00:03:23,423 --> 00:03:24,923
[SPEAKER_02]: Absolutely, yeah.

75
00:03:26,284 --> 00:03:27,525
[SPEAKER_02]: Your children were born up there?

76
00:03:27,785 --> 00:03:29,486
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

77
00:03:29,986 --> 00:03:32,507
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you lived in Madison until about 1930?

78
00:03:32,547 --> 00:03:33,128
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

79
00:03:33,608 --> 00:03:35,209
[SPEAKER_02]: And then where'd you move to?

80
00:03:36,369 --> 00:03:40,971
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, from there I went to...

81
00:03:41,051 --> 00:03:41,972
[SPEAKER_01]: I lived in St. Louis.

82
00:03:43,132 --> 00:03:44,093
[SPEAKER_01]: I had a sister there.

83
00:03:45,097 --> 00:03:47,158
[SPEAKER_02]: At your home, your parents home?

84
00:03:47,178 --> 00:03:48,918
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I lived with her.

85
00:03:52,079 --> 00:03:52,719
[SPEAKER_01]: And then what?

86
00:03:52,959 --> 00:03:53,740
[SPEAKER_01]: Then she died.

87
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:55,540
[SPEAKER_01]: I lived in Omaha.

88
00:03:59,541 --> 00:04:00,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Then I lived in Atlanta.

89
00:04:03,492 --> 00:04:08,414
[SPEAKER_01]: I lived in Cincinnati one year when I played over there and I came back to Columbus.

90
00:04:08,554 --> 00:04:13,256
[SPEAKER_02]: You really moved around and lived where you played and didn't have a home that you went back to?

91
00:04:13,276 --> 00:04:15,618
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I always lived where I played.

92
00:04:16,158 --> 00:04:18,799
[SPEAKER_00]: You lived in Columbus a long time?

93
00:04:18,899 --> 00:04:19,319
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

94
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:23,121
[SPEAKER_00]: You lived in Columbus a long time?

95
00:04:23,481 --> 00:04:28,844
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I came to Columbus in 32 and I stayed in Columbus until 42.

96
00:04:31,623 --> 00:04:34,104
[SPEAKER_02]: Where did you live here in Columbus?

97
00:04:34,184 --> 00:04:36,005
[SPEAKER_01]: 3776 South 9th Street.

98
00:04:36,065 --> 00:04:36,766
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it a home?

99
00:04:37,026 --> 00:04:38,907
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, I own a place down there.

100
00:04:38,927 --> 00:04:39,728
[SPEAKER_01]: You own a home?

101
00:04:39,788 --> 00:04:40,328
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

102
00:04:44,510 --> 00:04:45,691
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that was convenient.

103
00:04:46,071 --> 00:04:46,691
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, it was.

104
00:04:47,112 --> 00:04:48,072
[SPEAKER_02]: What'd you do in the winters?

105
00:04:49,313 --> 00:04:50,073
[SPEAKER_02]: Hunt and fish.

106
00:04:51,254 --> 00:04:52,915
[SPEAKER_01]: Around here or did you go up north?

107
00:04:52,955 --> 00:04:55,176
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I went just around here at all.

108
00:04:55,576 --> 00:04:56,797
[SPEAKER_01]: But I had a job.

109
00:04:56,917 --> 00:04:58,158
[SPEAKER_01]: I had a job as a sailor.

110
00:04:59,287 --> 00:05:05,369
[SPEAKER_01]: I followed the ball players, I sold beer, but I didn't like that job too well.

111
00:05:06,090 --> 00:05:09,571
[SPEAKER_01]: I sold a lot of... How did you get that job?

112
00:05:10,311 --> 00:05:27,318
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I went up the bowling alley one day, to bowl, and there was a man up there by the name of Frank Nagle, and Jeff Hart Yeager, I think was his first name, owned the Yeager Machine Company, and they had a distributor for beer.

113
00:05:28,618 --> 00:05:37,025
[SPEAKER_01]: So, Nate asked me if I wanted to work, and I said, yeah, I wanted to work with him.

114
00:05:37,065 --> 00:05:41,528
[SPEAKER_01]: Went out in the country and took a load of beer on a truck.

115
00:05:42,449 --> 00:05:44,050
[SPEAKER_01]: Went out and sold it all.

116
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:45,891
[SPEAKER_01]: Come back, I sold lots of beer for him.

117
00:05:46,992 --> 00:05:48,673
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you do this a number of years?

118
00:05:49,854 --> 00:05:52,216
[SPEAKER_01]: No, just that one year was all.

119
00:05:53,537 --> 00:05:54,478
[SPEAKER_01]: When would that have been?

120
00:05:55,535 --> 00:06:00,217
[SPEAKER_01]: That was in 1933.

121
00:06:00,577 --> 00:06:01,958
[SPEAKER_01]: After the 33 season?

122
00:06:01,998 --> 00:06:02,358
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

123
00:06:03,059 --> 00:06:04,539
[SPEAKER_01]: You didn't like South beer?

124
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,860
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I didn't like it.

125
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:11,222
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't like the idea of hanging around those beer guys too much.

126
00:06:11,983 --> 00:06:16,065
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, you go in and some guy says, here, buy a beer, drink one.

127
00:06:16,585 --> 00:06:20,346
[SPEAKER_01]: If I drank it all, I'd probably weigh 800 pounds.

128
00:06:24,793 --> 00:06:28,055
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, did you have any other jobs in off-seasons after that?

129
00:06:28,676 --> 00:06:32,098
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I worked at the A-Machine, I mean, yeah.

130
00:06:33,119 --> 00:06:41,204
[SPEAKER_01]: I worked over at, uh... Jeffery's Machine Company.

131
00:06:41,224 --> 00:06:42,665
[SPEAKER_01]: I worked up there for about...

132
00:06:42,885 --> 00:06:43,746
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is this?

133
00:06:43,766 --> 00:06:44,967
[SPEAKER_01]: Jeffery's Manufacturing Company, yeah.

134
00:06:44,987 --> 00:06:45,647
[SPEAKER_02]: That's in Columbus?

135
00:06:45,747 --> 00:06:47,168
[SPEAKER_01]: I was, uh, running a... Jeffery's.

136
00:06:47,508 --> 00:06:47,929
[SPEAKER_01]: Jeffery's.

137
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:49,530
[SPEAKER_00]: Jeffery's Manufacturing Company.

138
00:06:50,758 --> 00:06:56,841
[SPEAKER_01]: I was running a beer cart making these sprockets for the general U.S. tank.

139
00:06:57,762 --> 00:07:00,423
[SPEAKER_01]: I worked there for what one winter we called.

140
00:07:00,483 --> 00:07:02,364
[SPEAKER_01]: I was in about 37 I think.

141
00:07:02,544 --> 00:07:03,385
[SPEAKER_01]: No, 36.

142
00:07:17,675 --> 00:07:19,497
[SPEAKER_02]: You just liked hunting fish too much, didn't you?

143
00:07:19,677 --> 00:07:19,957
[SPEAKER_02]: Huh?

144
00:07:20,458 --> 00:07:22,540
[SPEAKER_02]: You liked hunting fish too much, didn't you?

145
00:07:24,201 --> 00:07:29,186
[SPEAKER_02]: Did your wife and family go with you on your trips during the season?

146
00:07:29,386 --> 00:07:29,666
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

147
00:07:31,828 --> 00:07:38,574
[SPEAKER_01]: They always had it arranged where if you could talk Ricky out of it, the money's transportation for your family.

148
00:07:39,555 --> 00:07:41,877
[SPEAKER_01]: But he was a little rough to deal with, I mean.

149
00:07:44,162 --> 00:07:52,169
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you, did all the Cardinal Minor League players sign with Ricky, deal with him directly?

150
00:07:52,649 --> 00:08:00,996
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, they signed him, but if you wouldn't sign, why, they'd get ahold of business manager and call Ricky up, see him, speak to him in the town and want to know why you wouldn't sign him.

151
00:08:01,657 --> 00:08:02,738
[SPEAKER_01]: Give you a lecture.

152
00:08:02,758 --> 00:08:05,160
[SPEAKER_01]: Give you a lecture about this and that.

153
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:08,102
[SPEAKER_01]: Pretty smart baseball man, as he was.

154
00:08:08,122 --> 00:08:11,005
[SPEAKER_01]: He knows the game's made of these, but nobody's monkey.

155
00:08:11,999 --> 00:08:15,481
[SPEAKER_02]: I talked to somebody, though, who played under him, said he wasn't a very good manager.

156
00:08:16,041 --> 00:08:18,142
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't know about his manager.

157
00:08:19,363 --> 00:08:20,783
[SPEAKER_02]: He talked to pretty good folks.

158
00:08:23,384 --> 00:08:28,927
[SPEAKER_02]: Forgotten, but somebody did play under him for a year or two.

159
00:08:28,967 --> 00:08:30,608
[SPEAKER_01]: As a business manager.

160
00:08:30,628 --> 00:08:32,109
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

161
00:08:32,129 --> 00:08:34,570
[SPEAKER_01]: I remember one time we had a meeting here in the clubhouse.

162
00:08:36,278 --> 00:08:37,859
[SPEAKER_01]: That's when we had a good ball problem.

163
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:42,902
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, when I played with the Redbirds, they were all good ballers.

164
00:08:43,863 --> 00:08:52,828
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he told me one day, he said, if I had nine ball players like Nick Cullip, he said, I wouldn't worry about nothing.

165
00:08:52,848 --> 00:08:54,089
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, that's all I'd want.

166
00:08:55,370 --> 00:08:59,892
[SPEAKER_01]: So, at the end of the season, he sent all these ball players to the big leagues, see?

167
00:09:00,533 --> 00:09:02,594
[SPEAKER_01]: But he left the old Cullip right here in Columbus.

168
00:09:03,668 --> 00:09:06,932
[SPEAKER_01]: So I said, well, I said, this spring I'm going to find out something.

169
00:09:08,274 --> 00:09:09,795
[SPEAKER_01]: So I held out for more money.

170
00:09:10,697 --> 00:09:14,141
[SPEAKER_01]: And I was already into Avon Park in the spring training.

171
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:18,522
[SPEAKER_01]: So Ricky come to town, and I was back in the field plowing.

172
00:09:19,083 --> 00:09:25,107
[SPEAKER_01]: Come down with that guy driving his car, you know, that red automobile, dust flying.

173
00:09:25,127 --> 00:09:26,428
[SPEAKER_01]: So I said, well, here he come.

174
00:09:27,028 --> 00:09:28,849
[SPEAKER_01]: He come down and said, what are you doing?

175
00:09:30,150 --> 00:09:31,251
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm like, what do you think I'm doing?

176
00:09:31,271 --> 00:09:32,011
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm flying a kite.

177
00:09:32,071 --> 00:09:34,033
[SPEAKER_01]: I got kind of smart with him, you know.

178
00:09:34,073 --> 00:09:36,414
[SPEAKER_01]: He didn't want to give me any money.

179
00:09:36,434 --> 00:09:39,176
[SPEAKER_01]: So he said, when are you going to spring training?

180
00:09:39,216 --> 00:09:40,457
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, when you give me some money.

181
00:09:42,558 --> 00:09:44,480
[SPEAKER_01]: And he said, well, I can't give you any more money.

182
00:09:46,532 --> 00:09:49,113
[SPEAKER_01]: And I said, well, I'll tell you something, Mr. Rickey.

183
00:09:49,153 --> 00:09:54,496
[SPEAKER_01]: In the statement you made, he said, if you had nine ball players like Nick Colton, you wouldn't worry about nothing.

184
00:09:55,317 --> 00:09:55,937
[SPEAKER_01]: Isn't that right?

185
00:09:56,397 --> 00:09:58,778
[SPEAKER_01]: And he said, do this priest.

186
00:09:58,838 --> 00:10:00,639
[SPEAKER_01]: And I said, nah, you certainly did.

187
00:10:01,660 --> 00:10:02,960
[SPEAKER_01]: And he said, how much money you want?

188
00:10:03,821 --> 00:10:05,142
[SPEAKER_01]: And I told him.

189
00:10:05,182 --> 00:10:11,785
[SPEAKER_01]: So we went right in the house, called up Al Bannister, signed Colton, get him on the plane right away.

190
00:10:12,161 --> 00:10:13,962
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I got a kick out of that.

191
00:10:14,002 --> 00:10:16,564
[SPEAKER_01]: He never swore he was a writer, did he?

192
00:10:18,225 --> 00:10:19,906
[SPEAKER_02]: You'd forgotten he said that, huh?

193
00:10:21,708 --> 00:10:22,388
[SPEAKER_02]: That's interesting.

194
00:10:24,009 --> 00:10:25,891
[SPEAKER_02]: Al Bannister, who was he?

195
00:10:26,171 --> 00:10:31,274
[SPEAKER_02]: He was the general manager of all the programs.

196
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:38,399
[SPEAKER_02]: Was he the general manager all these years in the 30s?

197
00:10:38,479 --> 00:10:38,820
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

198
00:10:38,980 --> 00:10:40,561
[SPEAKER_01]: They took him to St. Louis and made him

199
00:10:41,692 --> 00:10:45,795
[SPEAKER_01]: He was the supervisor of all the ballparks, you know, on equipment and things like that.

200
00:10:46,476 --> 00:10:49,318
[SPEAKER_01]: But since then he has passed away.

201
00:10:50,118 --> 00:10:51,799
[SPEAKER_01]: Who took over from him here?

202
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:53,421
[SPEAKER_01]: Red Trotman.

203
00:10:57,263 --> 00:11:02,207
[SPEAKER_02]: Did Billy Southwest stay as manager all the years you were here?

204
00:11:02,827 --> 00:11:06,690
[SPEAKER_01]: He has a farm up here at Sunbury.

205
00:11:06,730 --> 00:11:07,931
[SPEAKER_01]: He died not too long ago.

206
00:11:11,815 --> 00:11:15,217
[SPEAKER_01]: It's been several years, I think, since he died.

207
00:11:15,317 --> 00:11:17,838
[SPEAKER_02]: Years, I would say.

208
00:11:17,878 --> 00:11:19,679
